    "lesson_id": "001",
    "trigger_word": "bonjour",
    "trigger_card_number": 1,
    "title": "LESSON 1: FRENCH PRONUNCIATION",
    "header_color": "green",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 4,
        "content": [
          "Bienvenue! French spelling looks tricky",
          "but the sounds are very consistent.",
          "",
          "a = 'ah' as in father                Press 1",
          "   la, ça, table",
          "",
          "é = 'ay' as in day (closed, sharp)   Press 2",
          "   café, été, désolé",
          "",
          "è/ê = 'eh' as in bet (open, softer)  Press 3",
          "   mère, père, être",
          "",
          "i = 'ee' as in machine               Press 4",
          "   ici, midi, merci",
          "",
          "o/ô = 'oh' as in note                Press 5",
          "   mot, vélo, hôtel"
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Leçon un",
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "La. Ça. Table.",
          "2": "Café. Été. Désolé.",
          "3": "Mère. Père. Être.",
          "4": "Ici. Midi. Merci.",
          "5": "Mot. Vélo. Hôtel."
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 4,
        "content": [
          "NASAL VOWELS — air through the nose,",
          "say the vowel but don't finish the n/m:",
          "",
          "an/en = nasal 'ah'                   Press 1",
          "   France, enfant, dans",
          "",
          "in/ain/ein = nasal 'eh'              Press 2",
          "   vin, pain, main",
          "",
          "on = nasal 'oh'                      Press 3",
          "   bon, maison, non",
          "",
          "un = nasal 'uh' (merges with 'in'    Press 4",
          "for many speakers)",
          "   un, lundi, parfum",
          "",
          "RULE: after a vowel, n/m usually isn't",
          "pronounced — it just nasalizes the vowel."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "France. Enfant. Dans.",
          "2": "Vin. Pain. Main.",
          "3": "Bon. Maison. Non.",
          "4": "Un. Lundi. Parfum."
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 3,
        "total_pages": 4,
        "content": [
          "CONSONANTS that differ from English:",
          "",
          "h = always SILENT                    Press 1",
          "   habiter, homme, heure",
          "",
          "c before e/i/y = soft 's'            Press 2",
          "   ici, cinéma, merci",
          "c before a/o/u = hard 'k'            Press 3",
          "   café, comme, cousin",
          "ç = always soft 's' (any vowel)      Press 4",
          "   ça, français, garçon",
          "",
          "g before e/i/y = soft (like 'zh')    Press 5",
          "   âge, manger, gilet",
          "g before a/o/u = hard 'g' in 'go'    Press 6",
          "   gauche, gomme, légume",
          "gn = like 'ny' in canyon             Press 7",
          "   montagne, gagner, ligne"
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Habiter. Homme. Heure.",
          "2": "Ici. Cinéma. Merci.",
          "3": "Café. Comme. Cousin.",
          "4": "Ça. Français. Garçon.",
          "5": "Âge. Manger. Gilet.",
          "6": "Gauche. Gomme. Légume.",
          "7": "Montagne. Gagner. Ligne."
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 4,
        "total_pages": 4,
        "content": [
          "SILENT FINAL CONSONANTS — most word-",
          "final consonants are NOT pronounced:",
          "",
          "trop, beaucoup, nez, gros            Press 1",
          "(final p, p, z, s = silent)",
          "",
          "EXCEPTION — 'CaReFuL' letters ARE     Press 2",
          "pronounced at the end of a word:",
          "c, r, f, l → avec, professeur, chef,",
          "animal",
          "",
          "STRESS: always falls on the LAST",
          "syllable of the word or phrase —",
          "much simpler than Spanish or English.",
          "",
          "Two more sounds get their own lessons",
          "later: ÉLISION (l'ami) and LIAISON",
          "(les amis), on the cards that need them."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Trop. Beaucoup. Nez. Gros.",
          "2": "Avec. Professeur. Chef. Animal."
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "002",
    "trigger_word": "âge",
    "trigger_card_number": 8,
    "title": "LESSON 2: READING A CARD",
    "header_color": "green",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "Every French card shows the article",
          "color-coded by gender — glance,",
          "don't guess:",
          "",
          "le = masculine (shown in BLUE)       Press 1",
          "   le nom, le pays, le métier",
          "",
          "la = feminine (shown in MAGENTA)     Press 2",
          "   la nationalité, la famille",
          "",
          "STRATEGY: never learn a noun alone —",
          "always learn it WITH its colored",
          "article. The color is the fastest",
          "way to know le vs la at a glance."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Leçon deux",
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "le nom, le pays, le métier",
          "2": "la nationalité, la famille"
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "ÉLISION — before a vowel sound, le/la",
          "drop their vowel and become l':",
          "",
          "le âge  →  l'âge                     Press 1",
          "la adresse → l'adresse",
          "",
          "The apostrophe keeps the gender",
          "color underneath — l'âge shows",
          "BLUE, l'adresse shows MAGENTA — so",
          "you still know the gender at a glance.",
          "",
          "Cards flag this with Elides: true.",
          "Elides: false means the article",
          "stays whole: le héros, la honte",
          "(more on those later — some words",
          "starting with h block élision)."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "l'âge, l'adresse"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "003",
    "trigger_word": "madame",
    "trigger_card_number": 18,
    "title": "LESSON 3: TU VS VOUS",
    "header_color": "green",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "French has TWO words for 'you':",
          "",
          "TU = informal — friends, family,     Press 1",
          "children, people your own age",
          "   Tu es prêt ? (Are you ready?)",
          "",
          "VOUS = formal AND plural —           Press 2",
          "strangers, elders, work, or more",
          "than one person",
          "   Vous êtes prêt ? (Are you ready?)",
          "",
          "You already used vous in 's'il vous",
          "plaît' — the formal 'please', really",
          "'if it pleases you (formal)'.",
          "",
          "VOUS reuses the verb form you'd use",
          "for a GROUP — no new conjugation to",
          "learn, just a new use for it."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Leçon trois",
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "tu es prêt",
          "2": "vous êtes prêt, s'il vous plaît"
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "WHEN IN DOUBT, USE VOUS:",
          "",
          "Starting with vous is always safe.   Press 1",
          "Someone may invite you to switch:",
          "'On peut se tutoyer' (We can use tu)",
          "",
          "Address strangers with a title:      Press 2",
          "Bonjour, madame. / Bonjour, monsieur.",
          "",
          "Switching tu→vous mid-conversation",
          "can sound cold; vous→tu is the normal",
          "direction, usually offered, not",
          "assumed."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "on peut se tutoyer",
          "2": "bonjour madame, bonjour monsieur"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "004",
    "trigger_word": "être",
    "trigger_card_number": 76,
    "title": "LESSON 4: PRESENT TENSE",
    "header_color": "green",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 3,
        "content": [
          "French verbs come in 3 families:",
          "-ER (parler)  -IR (finir)  -RE (vendre)",
          "",
          "-ER is the biggest family — most new",
          "verbs are -ER. Drop -er, add:",
          "",
          "je parle            = I speak        Press 1",
          "tu parles           = you speak",
          "il/elle parle       = he/she speaks",
          "nous parlons        = we speak",
          "vous parlez         = you speak (fml/pl.)",
          "ils/elles parlent   = they speak",
          "",
          "parle/parles/parle/parlent all SOUND",
          "the same — only nous and vous change",
          "the sound. Listen for the ending."
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Leçon quatre",
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "je parle, tu parles, il parle, nous parlons, vous parlez, ils parlent"
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 3,
        "content": [
          "-IR verbs (finir = to finish):       Press 1",
          "",
          "je finis            = I finish",
          "tu finis            = you finish",
          "il/elle finit       = he/she finishes",
          "nous finissons      = we finish",
          "vous finissez       = you finish",
          "ils/elles finissent = they finish",
          "",
          "-RE verbs (vendre = to sell):        Press 2",
          "",
          "je vends            = I sell",
          "tu vends            = you sell",
          "il/elle vend        = he/she sells",
          "nous vendons        = we sell",
          "ils/elles vendent   = they sell"
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "je finis, tu finis, il finit, nous finissons, vous finissez, ils finissent",
          "2": "je vends, tu vends, il vend, nous vendons, ils vendent"
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 3,
        "total_pages": 3,
        "content": [
          "THE BIG 4 — irregular, and used",
          "constantly. Memorize these cold:",
          "",
          "ÊTRE (to be):                        Press 1",
          "suis, es, est, sommes, êtes, sont",
          "",
          "AVOIR (to have):                     Press 2",
          "ai, as, a, avons, avez, ont",
          "",
          "ALLER (to go):                       Press 3",
          "vais, vas, va, allons, allez, vont",
          "",
          "FAIRE (to do/make):                  Press 4",
          "fais, fais, fait, faisons, faites, font",
          "",
          "These four also build other tenses",
          "later (futur proche, passé composé)",
          "— learn them well now."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "suis, es, est, sommes, êtes, sont",
          "2": "ai, as, a, avons, avez, ont",
          "3": "vais, vas, va, allons, allez, vont",
          "4": "fais, fais, fait, faisons, faites, font"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "005",
    "trigger_word": "essayer",
    "trigger_card_number": 99,
    "title": "LESSON 5: NEGATION",
    "header_color": "green",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "NE...PAS wraps AROUND the verb —",
          "it's a sandwich, not a single word:",
          "",
          "Je ne parle pas.                     Press 1",
          "(I don't speak / I'm not speaking.)",
          "",
          "Je ne suis pas prêt.                 Press 2",
          "(I'm not ready.)",
          "",
          "In casual spoken French, 'ne' is",
          "often dropped: 'Je parle pas' — but",
          "always write both parts in Core.",
          "",
          "With an infinitive, both pieces move",
          "together, right before it:            Press 3",
          "Je préfère ne pas essayer.",
          "(I prefer not to try.)"
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Leçon cinq",
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "je ne parle pas",
          "2": "je ne suis pas prêt",
          "3": "je préfère ne pas essayer"
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "OTHER NEGATIONS use the same",
          "ne...___ sandwich, different word:",
          "",
          "ne...plus = no more/not anymore      Press 1",
          "   Je n'ai plus faim.",
          "",
          "ne...jamais = never                  Press 2",
          "   Je ne mange jamais de viande.",
          "",
          "ne...rien = nothing                  Press 3",
          "   Je ne vois rien.",
          "",
          "ne...personne = nobody               Press 4",
          "   Je ne connais personne ici.",
          "",
          "Notice: ne elides to n' before a",
          "vowel sound — n'ai, n'aime, n'est."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "je n'ai plus faim",
          "2": "je ne mange jamais de viande",
          "3": "je ne vois rien",
          "4": "je ne connais personne ici"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "lesson_id": "006",
    "trigger_word": "heure",
    "trigger_card_number": 151,
    "title": "LESSON 6: IL Y A & TELLING TIME",
    "header_color": "green",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 3,
        "content": [
          "IL Y A = there is / there are —",
          "one phrase, doesn't change for",
          "singular or plural:",
          "",
          "Il y a un problème.                  Press 1",
          "(There's a problem.)",
          "Il y a des livres.                   Press 2",
          "(There are books.)",
          "",
          "QUESTION — just flip the tone up,",
          "or add est-ce que:",
          "Il y a un problème ?                 Press 3",
          "(Is there a problem?)",
          "",
          "NEGATIVE — the usual ne...pas",
          "sandwich around 'a':",
          "Il n'y a pas de problème.            Press 4",
          "(There's no problem.)"
        ],
        "pronunciation": "Leçon six",
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "il y a un problème",
          "2": "il y a des livres",
          "3": "il y a un problème ?",
          "4": "il n'y a pas de problème"
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 3,
        "content": [
          "TELLING TIME uses il est + heure(s):",
          "",
          "Il est une heure.                    Press 1",
          "(It's one o'clock.)",
          "Il est deux heures.                  Press 2",
          "(It's two o'clock.)",
          "",
          "'Une heure' is singular, so no s.",
          "From deux heures on, heure takes -s.",
          "",
          "Il est midi. / Il est minuit.        Press 3",
          "(It's noon. / It's midnight.)",
          "",
          "Il est deux heures dix.              Press 4",
          "(2:10)",
          "Il est trois heures moins dix.       Press 5",
          "(2:50)"
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "il est une heure",
          "2": "il est deux heures",
          "3": "il est midi, il est minuit",
          "4": "il est deux heures dix",
          "5": "il est trois heures moins dix"
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 3,
        "total_pages": 3,
        "content": [
          "LIAISON — a silent final consonant",
          "wakes up before the next vowel:",
          "",
          "deux heures → deux_heures [z]        Press 1",
          "trois heures → trois_heures [z]      Press 2",
          "six heures → six_heures [z]          Press 3",
          "dix heures → dix_heures [z]          Press 4",
          "",
          "Beyond numbers, the same thing:",
          "",
          "un an → un_an [n]                    Press 5",
          "les amis → les_amis [z]              Press 6",
          "très utile → très_utile [z]          Press 7",
          "",
          "Lesson 8 returns to liaison in full."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "deux heures",
          "2": "trois heures",
          "3": "six heures",
          "4": "dix heures",
          "5": "un an",
          "6": "les amis",
          "7": "très utile"
        }
      }
    ]
  }
